WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.464
Raj: Okay, the patch inventory is generated automatically. Friday's two pilot hosts passed validation.

2
00:00:07.464 --> 00:00:15.576
Lukas: Does the inventory show reboot requirements too? Package installation alone doesn't establish running kernel state.

3
00:00:15.576 --> 00:00:22.897
Raj: Yes, installed and running versions appear separately. A pending reboot stays clearly flagged.

4
00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:29.977
Hannah: Did each pilot include a smoke test? Include service readiness after the reboot.

5
00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:37.105
Anika: Yes, both service checks passed on Friday. No remaining issue from those pilot hosts.

6
00:00:37.105 --> 00:00:45.145
Priya: Just to confirm, staged rollout still applies, right? Two hosts don't prove fleet-wide compatibility.

7
00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:52.009
Lukas: Correct, driver variants still need coverage. Which maintenance window covers the next group?

8
00:00:52.009 --> 00:00:59.114
Raj: Wednesday evening, subject to the pending approval. What's the ETA from the application owner?

9
00:00:59.114 --> 00:01:06.698
Hannah: They haven't committed to an approval time. Show that dependency instead of assuming Wednesday.

10
00:01:06.698 --> 00:01:14.090
Priya: So, prepare roughly ten candidate hosts today. Don't schedule reboots before that approval lands.

